    "title": "SpaceX launches Starlink 10-62 mission from Cape Canaveral, Florida",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 1:59 p.m. ETCrowds on the beach in Cocoa Beach watch the launch of the SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket carrying 29 Starlink satellites. The rocket launched at 10:47 a.m. EST on Sunday, March 22 from Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station.Malcolm Denemark,FLORIDA TODAYAn alligator and several manatees relax as a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket lifts off from Cape Canaveral Space Force Station March 22, 2026, carrying 29 Starlink satellites. Craig Bailey, FLORIDA TODAY via USA TODAY NETWORKCraig Bailey, FLORIDA TODAYThe 10:47 a.m. March 22 launch of the SpaceX Starlink 10-62 mission from Cape Canaveral Space Force Station, as seen from Viera.Tim Shortt/ FLORIDA TODAYA SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket lifts off from Cape Canaveral Space Force Station March 22, 2026, carrying 29 Starlink satellites. Craig Bailey, FLORIDA TODAY via USA TODAY NETWORKCraig Bailey, FLORIDA TODAYCrowds on the beach in Cocoa Beach watch the launch of the SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket carrying 29 Starlink satellites. The rocket launched at 10:47 a.m. EST on Sunday, March 22 from Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station.Malcolm Denemark,FLORIDA TODAYCrowds on the beach in Cocoa Beach watch the launch of the SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket carrying 29 Starlink satellites. The rocket launched at 10:47 a.m. EST on Sunday, March 22 from Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station.Malcolm Denemark,FLORIDA TODAYCrowds on the beach in Cocoa Beach watch the launch of the SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket carrying 29 Starlink satellites. The rocket launched at 10:47 a.m. EST on Sunday, March 22 from Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station.Malcolm Denemark,FLORIDA TODAYA SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket lifts off from Cape Canaveral Space Force Station March 22, 2026, carrying 29 Starlink satellites. Craig Bailey, FLORIDA TODAY via USA TODAY NETWORKCraig Bailey, FLORIDA TODAYCrowds on the beach in Cocoa Beach watch the launch of the SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket carrying 29 Starl